      "text": "$n$ the number of length to walk.\n$b_n * n = 1000\\longrightarrow (1)$\n$m$ the number of perimeter to walk.\n$P * m = 1000 \\longrightarrow (2)$\n$P = 2b + 2l$\n$(2)$ $P*10 = 2b +2l*10= 1000 \\longrightarrow$ $10b + 10l = 1000 \\longrightarrow$ $b + l = 100 \\longrightarrow$ $(3)$\n$(1) - 25 * (3) \\longrightarrow$ $n * b - 25b - 25l = 10000 \\longrightarrow$ $n\\cdot b - 25b = 10000 \\longrightarrow$ $b (n-25) = 10000 \\longrightarrow$ $b = \\dfrac{10000}{n-25}\\longrightarrow$\n$(3) * 25 \\longrightarrow$ $25b + 25l = 2500 \\longrightarrow$ $25 (b + l) = 2500 \\longrightarrow$ $b + l = 100 \\longrightarrow$ $(3)$\n$b = \\dfrac{10000}{n-25}\\longrightarrow$ $25 (b + l) = 2500 \\longrightarrow$ $b + l = 100 \\longrightarrow$\n$\\dfrac{10000}{n-25} + l = 100\\longrightarrow l = 100 - \\dfrac{10000}{n-25} \\longrightarrow$\nSubstituting $l$ in $(2)$: $P*10 = (2*b + 2*l) * 10 = 2b + 2l* 10= 1000\\longrightarrow$ $2* {2*}(\\dfrac{10000}{n-25} - \\dfrac{10000}{n-25}) + 2*\\dfrac{10000}{n-25}\\longrightarrow$ $2* \\dfrac{40000}{n-25} + 2*\\dfrac{10000}{n-25}\\longrightarrow$ $ \\dfrac{80000 + 20000}{n-25}\\longrightarrow$ $ \\dfrac{100000}{n-25}\\longrightarrow$ $\\dfrac{100000}{n-25} = 1000\\longrightarrow$ $ 100000 = 1000(n-25)\\longrightarrow$ $100000 = 1000n -25000\\longrightarrow$ $100000 + 25000 = 1000n\\longrightarrow$ $125000 = 1000n\\longrightarrow$ $n = \\dfrac{125000}{1000}\\longrightarrow$ $n = 125$\nSubstituting $n$ in $(3):$ $b + l = 100 \\longrightarrow$ $b + l = 100 \\longrightarrow$ $125b + 125l = 12500\\longrightarrow$ $l = 100 - b\\longrightarrow$ $125b = 12500 - 125l\\longrightarrow$ $125b = 12500 - 125(100 - b)\\longrightarrow$ $125b = 12500 - 12500 + 125b\\longrightarrow$ $b = \\dfrac{-12500 + 12500}{125}\\longrightarrow$ $b = 100 - l\\longrightarrow$ $l = 100 -100\\longrightarrow$ $l = 0$\n*Substituting $n$ again in $(2)$, we now have: $l = 100 - \\dfrac{10000}{n-25} \\longrightarrow$ $l = 100 - \\dfrac{10000}{125 -25} \\longrightarrow$ $l = 100 - \\dfrac{10000}{100}\\longrightarrow$ $l = 100 - \\dfrac{10000}{100}\\longrightarrow$ $l = 100 - 100\\longrightarrow$ $l = -100 + 100\\longrightarrow$ $l = 100 - 100\\longrightarrow$ $l = 100 - 100\\longrightarrow$ $l = 100 - 10\\longrightarrow$ $l = 90$\n*Finally, we found $l = 90, b = 100 - l = 100 - 90 = 10 $\n$Area = ab = 90*10 = \\boxed{900}$ square meters.",
