      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine the dimensions of Mateen's rectangular backyard and then calculate its area. Let's denote the length of the backyard by \\( l \\) meters and the width by \\( w \\) meters.\n\nFirst, we are given that walking the length 25 times will equal 1000 meters:\n\\[\n25l = 1000\n\\]\nSolving for \\( l \\):\n\\[\nl = \\frac{1000}{25} = 40 \\text{ meters}\n\\]\n\nNext, we are given that walking the perimeter 10 times will also equal 1000 meters. The perimeter \\( P \\) of a rectangle is given by:\n\\[\nP = 2l + 2w\n\\]\nWe know that walking the perimeter 10 times is equivalent to walking the perimeter once 10 times:\n\\[\n10P = 1000\n\\]\nSubstituting the expression for \\( P \\):\n\\[\n10(2l + 2w) = 1000\n\\]\nSimplifying:\n\\[\n2l + 2w = 100\n\\]\nSince we already know \\( l = 40 \\):\n\\[\n2(40) + 2w = 100\n\\]\n\\[\n80 + 2w = 100\n\\]\nSolving for \\( w \\):\n\\[\n2w = 20\n\\]\n\\[\nw = 10 \\text{ meters}\n\\]\n\nNow that we have the dimensions of the backyard, we can calculate the area \\( A \\):\n\\[\nA = l \\times w = 40 \\times 10 = 400 \\text{ square meters}\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of Mateen's backyard is \\(\\boxed{400}\\) square meters.",
