    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "The distance Mateen walks when he walks the length 25 times is \\(25 \\times 1000 = 25000\\) meters. Therefore, this distance can also be written as \\(25 \\times 1000 = 25 \\times 10 \\times 100 = 250 \\times 100 = 25000\\) meters.\n\nSo, the length \\(L\\) of the backyard is \\(L = \\frac{25000}{25} = 1000\\) meters, and the width \\(W\\) is \\(W = \\frac{25000}{10} = 2500\\) meters.\n\nThe area \\(A\\) of the backyard is given by the formula \\(A = L \\times W = 1000 \\times 2500 = 2500000\\) square meters.\n\nThus, the area of Mateen's backyard is \\(\\boxed{2500000}\\) square meters.",
