    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the area of Mateen's backyard, we can use the information given to set up equations for both scenarios.\n\n1. **First Scenario:**\n   - Mateen needs to walk the length 25 times to cover 1000 meters.\n   - Let the length of the backyard be \\( L \\) meters.\n   - The total distance walked in this scenario is \\( 25L = 1000 \\) meters.\n   - Solving for \\( L \\):\n     \\[\n     L = \\frac{1000}{25} = 40 \\text{ meters}\n     \\]\n\n2. **Second Scenario:**\n   - Mateen needs to walk the perimeter 10 times to cover 1000 meters.\n   - Let the perimeter of the backyard be \\( P \\) meters.\n   - The total distance walked in this scenario is \\( 10P = 1000 \\) meters.\n   - Solving for \\( P \\):\n     \\[\n     P = \\frac{1000}{10} = 100 \\text{ meters}\n     \\]\n\nNow, we know the length \\( L = 40 \\) meters and the perimeter \\( P = 100 \\) meters. The perimeter of a rectangle is given by:\n\\[\nP = 2L + 2W\n\\]\nwhere \\( W \\) is the width of the backyard. Substituting the known values:\n\\[\n100 = 2(40) + 2W\n\\]\n\\[\n100 = 80 + 2W\n\\]\n\\[\n20 = 2W\n\\]\n\\[\nW = 10 \\text{ meters}\n\\]\n\nThe area \\( A \\) of the backyard is given by:\n\\[\nA = L \\times W\n\\]\nSubstituting the values of \\( L \\) and \\( W \\):\n\\[\nA = 40 \\times 10 = 400 \\text{ square meters}\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of Mateen's backyard is \\(\\boxed{400}\\) square meters.",
